          "title": "You'll want to know: 重要",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "重要 — zhòngyào — \"important\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "每天喝水很重要 měitiān hē shuǐ hěn zhòngyào — Drinking water every day is important."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "重要 (zhòngyào) is built from 重 'heavy' and 要, glossed 'to bind, to agree', both inherited from Middle Chinese, drjowngX and 'jiewH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription). How the pair came to mean important is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing things."
